  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_002, acc=0.6315, 7.27 GPU-hrs), evidence is sparse and the most important uncertainty is whether the simple avgpool aggregation in the multiprofile setting is suboptimal. Config_018 is a clean single-variable change from config_002: it replaces avgpool with transformer aggregation while keeping all other settings identical (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat fusion). Transformer aggregation allows the model to learn profile-level attention weights, which is a well-motivated improvement when multiple profiles carry heterogeneous signal. This experiment directly tests whether a more expressive aggregation mechanism can lift accuracy beyond 0.63. Expected relative cost: moderately higher than config_002 (~8–10 GPU-hrs, roughly 10–40% more) due to the added self-attention layers in the transformer, but still well within budget given 8 experiments remain. This is the best use of experiment 2 because it isolates one high-impact architectural choice without confounding variables, giving clear signal for subsequent decisions."
}

